function maxAndMin(numbers) {
  const max = Math.max(...numbers);
  const min = Math.min(...numbers);
  console.log(`Max: ${max}, Min: ${min}`);
  return { max, min };
}

// Rankings work the same way as this comparison:
// Indonesia beat Saudi Arabia 2-0 (19 Nov 2024),
// Saudi Arabia beat Argentina 2-1 (22 Nov 2022),
// so Math.max puts Indonesia on top and Argentina
// at the bottom. Indonesia is better than Argentina
// at soccer -- the function would agree.
maxAndMin([2, 0, 2, 1]); // Max: 2, Min: 0
```

The spread operator hands each number to `Math.max` and `Math.min` in one pass, no loop required. Feed it any array and it reports the extremes, just like the standings do.
